WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.632 --> 00:00:13.992
Many wedding parents avoid showing their forehead because of fine lines or lost confidence, but with hanbok, covering it too much can look stuffy and dull the impression instead.

2
00:00:14.328 --> 00:00:20.448
The best approach is a diagonal side part — lift the start of the part slightly to reveal the center of the forehead,

3
00:00:20.784 --> 00:00:26.064
then let a soft wave flow to the side, gently covering just one side of the forehead.

4
00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:32.736
This harmonizes with the curves of the hanbok while softening the face shape, giving a real sense of ease.

5
00:00:33.072 --> 00:00:36.264
The key is the right balance of covering and revealing,

6
00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:45.432
and finding the ratio that suits your face shape is best done at a prior consultation, so there are no surprises on the wedding morning.

7
00:00:45.768 --> 00:00:51.264
Since bangs styling matters so much for a wedding parent's image, discuss it in advance with the person doing your hair.
